From 64d715547730c1cbe9cc3030f55aa6fd4beba7b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sunwoong Joo <gomida@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:22:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] media, blink: deterministic video playback under
 --deterministic-capture

Patch 7 of the deterministic capture series.

- WebMediaPlayerImpl registers with CaptureMediaRegistry (platform/media,
  exposed as blink::WebCaptureMediaRegistry) and holds a kInstant virtual-time
  pauser from every play, pause, seek, rate change, suspend, resume and
  pipeline start until the media thread has absorbed it, no PipelineController
  operation is pending (new HasPendingOperation()) and a running, unsuspended
  pipeline has reached HAVE_FUTURE_DATA. loadedmetadata, canplay and the
  autoplay play() therefore land at the virtual time of the request.
- MainThreadSchedulerImpl does not fence task queues while virtual time is
  stopped in capture mode (neither on pause nor for queues created while
  paused); the pauser would otherwise deadlock on the fenced media callbacks.
  Delayed tasks stay gated by virtual time.
- VideoRendererImpl::Render waits, with the lock released, until the queued
  frames cover the render deadline or end of stream (10 s bound), cancelled
  before the sink stops; VideoFrameSubmitter renders [T, T+interval] for the
  BeginFrame at T; VideoFrameCompositor background rendering is off;
  MultiBufferDataSource seeks without the 20 ms delay that virtual time would
  gate.
- media/base/deterministic_capture.h: IsDeterministicCaptureMode().

Measured on 158 with a muted looping WebM: run-to-run identical hashes over
120 frames, and two chunks with pre-roll equal to the serial render frame by
frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
